<title>UK: Russia's Novorossiisk Black Sea oil port shut.</title>
<headline>Russia's Novorossiisk Black Sea oil port shut.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Black Sea oil terminal of Novorossiisk, Russia's main outlet to European markets, closed on Monday due to high winds and swell and stayed shut on Tuesday, a reliable shipping source said.</p>
<p>Novorossiisk shut at 1250 local time on Monday, leaving four crude tankers at anchor outside the port, the source added.</p>
<p>Other Black Sea ports at Odessa and Tuapse were open and operating normally as was Latvia's port of Ventspils on the Baltic, the source said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
